      <tei:div type="colophon" subtype="notes">
        <tei:p>This prayer by an unknown author is first found in <tei:hi rend="italic">Evening Service for the Sabbath from the Union Prayer Book (Newly Revised)</tei:hi> (1924), p. 45. (It also appears on the same page of the 1940 edition of the “newly revised” UPB.) The prayer is included as a third variation of a Reform synagogue’s Shabbat evening service, in the Amidah before the silent meditation. Rabbi Michael Satz of Temple B’nai Or (Morristown, New Jersey) affectionately refers to it as the “Coal Miner’s Prayer.”</tei:p>
      </tei:div>
